    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0648" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-25T13:00:00-05:00">October 25, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>548. Reference to your 1488, October 22, 9 a.m. and your 1508, October 23, 7
                    p.m., I greatly appreciate the information reported. Davis’<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d695-f1"/> instructions do not contemplate the advocacy of any
                    concrete course of action. In accordance with Article 7 of the Nine Power
                    Treaty, he is proceeding to Brussels for “full and frank communication” with the
                    other signatory powers, in the hope that together they may work out some plan
                    for finding an end to the conflict by agreement.</p>
                <p>Beyond the foregoing, I see no line that you could take usefully in your
                    conversations. We will advise you from day to day of any developments in our
                    consideration of the problem here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d695-f1" n="63" xml:id="d695-f1-content">
                <p>Norman H. Davis, American delegate to the Brussels Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
